WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back, John!
-Yeah, it´s great to be back.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So happy to see you.
Since you were last here,

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.672
you had a wonderful portrayal

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
of Winston Churchill
in "The Crown."

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.943
-Yes.
-Deservedly won an Emmy for it.

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:12.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I did.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That...

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:16.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, you´re
approaching a character

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:17.784
so many actors have played.

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:21.988
And you are an American so you
have to do the British accent.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
I heard you had
a way of approaching

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:26.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
your Winston Churchill voice
that is just very unique.

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:29.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, he was a unique man
in every way,

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.797
including the way he talked.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
I sort of --
I knew I had to

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:36.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
develop exactly
the right Winston Churchill.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
He had a very jowly face.
-Yes.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.641
-And I remembered Marlon Brando
in "The Godfather,"

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:44.878
and I thought, "Well, I´ll
stick something into my jowls."

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:48.181
I practiced this at home before
I went to England to join them.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
With a melon baller,
I created these

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
little apple balls
and stuck them in --

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:55.655
[ Laughter ]
And I just stared at the mirror.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.323
"I have nothing to offer."

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought, "I´ve got it!"
-Wow!

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:02.929
-I actually took a melon baller
with me to England.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-And arrived --

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:05.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you got
right through customs.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:06.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
They had no issue with it.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
I was not stopped.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
And took an apple to rehearsal
one day, and I said,

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:13.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I just want
to experiment with this."

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:18.978
And I dug out two apple balls
and put them in my jowls...

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-...and spoke a scene with it.

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:24.451
About 40 seconds in, my mouth --
It sounded great.

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.119
It sounded very Churchillian,

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:28.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
but my mouth
was full of apple juice.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Turns out
that was Churchillian, too.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
Winston Churchill famously

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
spit out apple juice
every 40 seconds.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-That´s what I said.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:37.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nickname.

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:39.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you´re playing
Will Ferrell´s father.

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
Perfect casting.
-Yes, it was so great.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.970
-And you are,
of the two fathers in this film,

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
you are
the more emotional father.

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:47.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s right.
-Yeah.

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:49.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mel Gibson
plays Mark Wahlberg´s dad.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:51.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, less emotional.
-Yes.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:54.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
He´s the sort of tough-love
kind of severe,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:59.586
hard-ass partner,
and I´m just sloppy sentimental,

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.988 size:81% position:41%
bursting with emotion.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Will and I,
as father and son,

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:08.194
we completely adore each other!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s fantastic.
I know you shot in Boston.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.499
You actually got to spend a week
together as a cast at a resort.

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:13.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that nice?
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.535 size:81% position:41%
-Because I know often
you actually do movies

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.637
and you don´t get to spend
that much time together.

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:20.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and it was good,
because we were all nervous.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we had --

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:26.146
We knew we had to turn into a
four-person ensemble very quick.

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:27.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was wonderful.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were in the Berkshires
for a week.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:33.453
We had to get as much snow as we
could before the Spring came.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:36.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was just
a great bonding week.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:38.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You had a great bonding,
it sounds like,

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:42.362
the entire time on the set when
you did the film "Footloose."

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
You actually
all hung out together.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:47.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that seems like a place --
You filmed that in Utah?

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:50.637
-We filmed it in Provo, Utah.

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:51.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:54.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A very conservative
little community.

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:55.708 size:81% position:41%
-Very "Footloose"-ian.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.710 size:75% position:38%
-Very "Footloose" --
Footlusion, I think.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.546
-Yeah, Footlusion, you´re right.
I apologize.

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:00.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Dianne Wiest and I,
were the oldsters.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:07.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were about 25 years younger
than we are now,

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:10.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we were the old --
the old folks.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.560
And all these fabulous
young kids -- Kevin Bacon

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:17.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Lori Singer
and Sarah Jessica Parker.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:21.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
Somehow or other, we, as a
sort of compensation for that,

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.369 size:88% position:44%
we became the wild ones.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, you and Dianne...
-Yes.

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...had to be cool
to show to the young people.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:28.908
-Yeah, yeah.
We all stayed in a motor court.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:33.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was sort of
the venerable older star,

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.815 size:88% position:44%
so I was given two rooms
with an adjoining door.

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh! Wow.
-So I threw the parties.

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:42.355
-We had, like, "Soul Train" --
You know, it was just crazy.

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.524 size:78% position:39%
And these young kids
thought we were nuts.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:46.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
But you had a good time.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:48.761
Did you ever get in trouble
with the Provo authorities?

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:49.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes!
-Oh, wow!

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:52.031
-Yeah, we flung off our clothes

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:53.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
and leaped into
the swimming pool one night.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that´s not --
I don´t think that´s

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
supposed to happen
at the Provo motor court.

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:59.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we got
a very stern dressing down

00:03:59.606 --> 00:04:00.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
from our producer
the next morning.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dan Melnick, so...
But that happens.

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hopefully, you learned
your lesson, John.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:07.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But it was odd,
´cause in "Footloose,"

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was the guy who wouldn´t
let anybody dance.

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:11.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, but turns out that
you´re too busy

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:14.053
doing other stuff,
skinny-dipping, to dance, yeah.

